@h1 Load a CSV into a table h1@

Render a real @code .csv code@ file as a table without hand-typing a single
row — the header line becomes the columns automatically. This is a focused
excerpt of
@a |href /docs/recipes/report-live-data/| A report with live data a@.

@h2 Step 1 — Point a source at the file h2@

Any program that emits CSV to standard output works; @code cat code@ is the
simplest. Wire it in @code wit.sources.json code@.

@@@pre
{
  "sources": {
    "downloads": { "run": ["cat", "data/downloads.csv"], "format": "csv" }
  }
}
pre@@@

@h2 Step 2 — Load and render it h2@

@@@pre
@load downloads load@

@table |rows @downloads|
pre@@@

@h2 Step 3 — Build h2@

@@@pre
wit build report.wit --sources wit.sources.json --allow-exec --fragment
pre@@@

@strong Result. strong@ The header row — say @code platform,downloads,change code@
— becomes three @code th code@ columns, and each remaining line becomes one
@code tr code@. The verified output starts:
@@@code <thead><tr><th>platform</th>… code@@@.

@h2 When you don't have a file h2@

Two forms cover the tables you type by hand, and both build green.

@h3 Inline rows h3@

The first inner array is the header.

@@@pre
@table |caption Corpus splits| |rows [[Group, A, B], [Teens, 8, 6.5]]|
pre@@@

@h3 Schema plus rows h3@

Supply the header separately, then feed a defined collection of records as the
body.

@@@pre
#corpus: [
  { split - Train, docs - 40k, tokens - 12.4M }
  { split - Dev, docs - 5k, tokens - 1.5M }
] !!

@table
  |schema [split, docs, tokens]|
  |rows @corpus|
table@
pre@@@

This renders a header of @code split code@, @code docs code@, @code tokens code@
and one row per record.

@h2 Pitfalls h2@

@ul
@li @strong Don't freeze the table. strong@ A frozen table written with a double
fence does @em not em@ resolve reference rows — use a plain
@@@code @table code@@@ so @@@code |rows @downloads| code@@@ is looked up. li@
@li @strong Commas still split records. strong@ A cell like @code 12.4M code@ is
fine, but @code Attention, Perception code@ inside a @@@code { } code@@@ record
reads as two fields. li@
ul@

@h2 See also h2@

@a |href /docs/recipes/report-live-data/| A report with live data a@ shows the
full data flow;
@a |href /docs/reference/core-vocabulary/| Core vocabulary a@ lists the table
nodes.
